Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Properties panels: rows and drop-downs optionally drawn
 like Nuke's

- sliderHandleBar (Appearance > Main Window; off by default, Natron's round handle as before): a slider's handle
  is a small upright bar in the slider colour, over a scale of thin ticks.
- knobDimensionButtonLast (off by default): the button splitting a value into its dimensions ("4" on a colour)
  comes after the colour swatch and wheel instead of before them.
- knobAnimationButton (off by default): each row of an animatable value (a number or a colour, alone on its line,
  outside the viewer) ends with a button opening its animation menu, the one a right-click on the value opens. The
  button is named KnobAnimationButton for stylesheets.
- pageTabNodeName (off by default): a node's first tab of controls, when its plug-in calls it "Controls", shows the
  node's kind instead (Grade, Blur).
- A drop-down (ComboBox) whose "flat" property is set shows its text and arrow without its box while it's at rest;
  nothing in Natron sets the property, so nothing changes unless a stylesheet layer or script does.
- Every new preference is read by name, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Core patch 0004 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/), written to be offered upstream as it is.

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the properties panels' knob rows).
Size: 6 files, 104 lines added, 10 removed.
upstream: not offered yet (Baptiste: keep the fork private for now).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
